target:    wp-slimstat.php
gate:      composer test:v5460-migration
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    init() calls LegacySettings5460::apply() exactly once
rationale: Renames the call so init() no longer delegates to the class the test exercises. The point of the extraction is one implementation; a block creeping back inline puts the test and production one file apart again, which is how the regression in M7 survived. The check reads wp-slimstat.php with comments blanked, because the comment above the call names the old guard while explaining why it is gone, and a raw scan found it there.
---
--- a/wp-slimstat.php
+++ b/wp-slimstat.php
@@ -293,3 +293,3 @@
         // plugins_loaded fires before the rule is registered on 'init' and wastes a DB write.
-        $_legacy = \SlimStat\Migration\LegacySettings5460::apply(
+        $_legacy = \SlimStat\Migration\LegacySettings5460::applyLegacy(
             self::$settings,
